theorem riccati_identity_of_jacobi {k u du ddu : ℝ → ℝ} {T : ℝ}
    (h : JacobiSolutionOn k u du ddu 0 T) (hpos : ∀ t ∈ Ioc 0 T, 0 < u t) :
    (∀ t ∈ Ioo 0 T, HasDerivAtR (fun s => du s / u s)
        ((ddu t * u t - du t ^ 2) / u t ^ 2) t) ∧
    (∀ t ∈ Ioo 0 T, (ddu t * u t - du t ^ 2) / u t ^ 2 + (du t / u t) ^ 2 / 1 + k t = 0) := by
  constructor
  · intro t ht
    have hune : u t ≠ 0 := ne_of_gt (hpos ⟨ht.1, ht.2.le⟩)
    have hd := (h.hasDerivAt_du ht).div (h.hasDerivAt_u ht) hune
    convert hd using 1
    ring
  · intro t ht
    have hune : u t ≠ 0 := ne_of_gt (hpos ⟨ht.1, ht.2.le⟩)
    rw [h.eq_secondDeriv ht]
    field_simp [hune]
    ring
```
Careful: `HasDerivAt.div` gives derivative `(ddu t * u t - du t * du t) / u t ^ 2`. Goal is `(ddu t * u t - du t ^ 2)/u t^2`. `convert hd using 1; ring` — the `using 1` produces goal for derivative equality; `ring` should close since du t ^ 2 = du t * du t.

Second: goal `(ddu t * u t - du t ^ 2)/u t^2 + (du t/u t)^2/1 + k t = 0`. With h.eq_secondDeriv: `ddu t = -(k t) * u t`. `rw [h.eq_secondDeriv ht]` rewrites ddu t. Then field_simp [hune]; ring. Should work.

